# US-422: real 404s for unknown URLs (fix soft 404).
#
# Cloudflare Pages resolution order: a Pages Function (functions/*, e.g. the
# /cert/:id and /verified/:handle SSR handlers, sitemaps, robots.txt) runs first,
# then an exact static-asset match (every prerendered public page —
# /, /pricing, /privacy, /grading/<slug>, … — is a dist/<route>/index.html file
# and is served directly), and only THEN are these _redirects rules evaluated.
#
# So the rules below only ever fire for paths with NO function and NO static
# file. We rewrite the known client-rendered app namespaces to the SPA shell
# (200) so client-side routing and authenticated deep links keep working, and
# send everything else to the 404 page with a real HTTP 404 status — junk and
# deleted URLs are no longer soft-404 indexed. First match wins.

# Client-rendered app shells (no prerender; behind auth or guest-only flows).
# Both the bare base (/dashboard) and the subtree (/dashboard/*) need a rule —
# the "/*" splat matches only paths that include the trailing slash.
/dashboard      /index.html   200
/dashboard/*    /index.html   200
/admin          /index.html   200
/admin/*        /index.html   200
/auth/*         /index.html   200
/login          /index.html   200
/signup         /index.html   200
/accept-invite  /index.html   200

# Genuinely unknown URL → real 404 (404.html carries meta robots noindex).
/*              /404.html     404
